('05a64e82-6ac1-5ebd-8c68-4326035adfd0','a398a101-dec6-5127-ade1-9850680eadf9',7,null,null,'spoken & written','a number that tells you where you can find the information you want in a book, on a map etc','[ countable ]',null,'عددی که به شما می گوید کجا می توانید اطلاعات مورد نظر خود را در کتاب، نقشه و غیره پیدا کنید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make reference to something Official reports made no reference to the incident.','there is a reference to something There are 32 references to eagles in the Bible.','a specific/direct/explicit reference (= mentioning something specifically/directly etc ) No specific reference was made to the race of the children.','an oblique reference (= not direct ) He added, in an oblique reference to the US, that ‘some countries could do more’.','a brief reference Brief references to the tragedy have appeared in the French press.','a passing reference (= one that you make while you are talking about something else ) He made only a passing reference to his injury.','frequent/constant/repeated references Medieval literature contains frequent references to insanity.','an occasional reference During the interview, he made only occasional references to his forthcoming autobiography.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a list of towns, each with a map reference","translation":"لیستی از شهرها، هر کدام با یک مرجع نقشه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001540449.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('197fee6a-f22e-5397-ae53-e537cd762fdc','60b8c84e-c19d-59b5-a3f1-bc6a8d091acb',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to mention another book, article etc that contains information connected with the subject you are writing about',null,null,'برای ذکر کتاب، مقاله و غیره دیگری که حاوی اطلاعات مرتبط با موضوعی است که در مورد آن می نویسید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The book does not reference anything written in the last 10 years.","translation":"این کتاب به هیچ چیزی که در 10 سال گذشته نوشته شده است اشاره نمی کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001540690.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
