('ae83ead7-18d4-5eb6-8e33-70d5555cca49','ef034c76-7cce-57ad-b193-0c456064d352',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a religious song of the type sung originally by African-Americans',null,null,'یک آهنگ مذهبی از نوع که در اصل توسط آمریکایی های آفریقایی تبار خوانده شده است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('373fa3c5-79ae-513f-a32f-77188a68bca2','e5a35b76-dd12-54e3-a3ec-3c1d37769d10',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a man who has been chosen to speak officially for a group, organization , or government',null,null,'سخنگو (مرد)؛ سخنگو (سازمان)؛ سخنگو (پیش‌سخنگو)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a White House spokesman","translation":"سخنگوی کاخ سفید","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000661172.mp3"},{"sentence":"a spokesman for the victims’ families","translation":"سخنگوی خانواده قربانیان","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000661175.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('ff2ed85f-c9c5-57f7-a59b-705cfc7a1371','bb2f5b36-2f63-555f-bc9c-c60ae5c6bf9e',1,null,null,'spoken & written','something you say or write, especially publicly or officially, to let people know your intentions or opinions , or to record facts','[ countable ]',null,'بیانیه، اظهار (رسمی)؛ بیانیه (دفتر)؛ اظهار (صورتی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make a statement (= say something, especially in public ) The minister will make a statement on the matter tomorrow.','give a statement (= make a statement, especially to the police ) He gave a statement to the police.','issue/release/put out a statement (= give a written statement to newspapers, TV etc ) The Russian Foreign Ministry issued a short statement saying the meeting was ‘useful’.','take/get a statement from somebody I asked the police why they didn’t take a statement from me four years ago.','withdraw your statement (= say that a statement you gave is not true ) She later withdrew her statement.','a short/brief statement Police last night issued a brief statement about the incident.','a clear statement (= giving an opinion clearly ) The article was a clear statement of his beliefs.','a sweeping statement (= one that is too general ) Researchers do not want to make any sweeping statements at this stage.','a false/misleading statement (= one that is not true ) She is accused of making false statements to obtain a passport.','an official statement The company is expected to make an official statement tomorrow.','a formal statement (= one you must sign to show that it is true ) You will be asked to make a formal statement.','a public statement (= one made in public ) We will be making no public statements about the matter.','a written statement One neighbour said in a written statement that she often heard a baby ‘crying for help’.','a prepared statement (= one that is prepared and then read out ) His solicitor read a prepared statement on his behalf.','a sworn statement (= one that you officially promise is true ) The reports were based on sworn statements of graduates of the terrorist training camp.','a policy statement (= one that explains a government policy ) In his first major policy statement to Parliament he promised to end corruption in public life.','a mission statement (= one in which an organization states its aims ) The role of a mission statement is to focus on the purpose of the organization.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"In an official statement, she formally announced her resignation.","translation":"وی در بیانیه ای رسمی استعفای خود را به طور رسمی اعلام کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001652158.mp3"},{"sentence":"the prime minister’s recent statements on Europe","translation":"اظهارات اخیر نخست وزیر درباره اروپا","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001652163.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('5e8d65f0-16ef-5f22-a4cf-47b67073e3b7','bb2f5b36-2f63-555f-bc9c-c60ae5c6bf9e',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a record showing amounts of money paid, received , owed etc','[ countable ]',null,'سابقه ای که مبالغ پرداختی، دریافتی، بدهی و غیره را نشان می دهد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make a statement (= say something, especially in public ) The minister will make a statement on the matter tomorrow.','give a statement (= make a statement, especially to the police ) He gave a statement to the police.','issue/release/put out a statement (= give a written statement to newspapers, TV etc ) The Russian Foreign Ministry issued a short statement saying the meeting was ‘useful’.','take/get a statement from somebody I asked the police why they didn’t take a statement from me four years ago.','withdraw your statement (= say that a statement you gave is not true ) She later withdrew her statement.','a short/brief statement Police last night issued a brief statement about the incident.','a clear statement (= giving an opinion clearly ) The article was a clear statement of his beliefs.','a sweeping statement (= one that is too general ) Researchers do not want to make any sweeping statements at this stage.','a false/misleading statement (= one that is not true ) She is accused of making false statements to obtain a passport.','an official statement The company is expected to make an official statement tomorrow.','a formal statement (= one you must sign to show that it is true ) You will be asked to make a formal statement.','a public statement (= one made in public ) We will be making no public statements about the matter.','a written statement One neighbour said in a written statement that she often heard a baby ‘crying for help’.','a prepared statement (= one that is prepared and then read out ) His solicitor read a prepared statement on his behalf.','a sworn statement (= one that you officially promise is true ) The reports were based on sworn statements of graduates of the terrorist training camp.','a policy statement (= one that explains a government policy ) In his first major policy statement to Parliament he promised to end corruption in public life.','a mission statement (= one in which an organization states its aims ) The role of a mission statement is to focus on the purpose of the organization.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the company’s annual financial statements","translation":"صورتهای مالی سالانه شرکت","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001782262.mp3"},{"sentence":"I haven’t received my bank statement for last month yet.","translation":"من هنوز صورت حساب بانکی ماه گذشته خود را دریافت نکرده ام.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001652173.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('c8121332-223f-5212-8627-7a2b99f55cba','bb2f5b36-2f63-555f-bc9c-c60ae5c6bf9e',3,null,null,'spoken & written','something you do, make, wear etc that causes people to have a certain opinion about you','[ countable ]',null,'کاری که انجام می دهید، می سازید، می پوشید و غیره که باعث می شود مردم نظر خاصی در مورد شما داشته باشند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make a statement (= say something, especially in public ) The minister will make a statement on the matter tomorrow.','give a statement (= make a statement, especially to the police ) He gave a statement to the police.','issue/release/put out a statement (= give a written statement to newspapers, TV etc ) The Russian Foreign Ministry issued a short statement saying the meeting was ‘useful’.','take/get a statement from somebody I asked the police why they didn’t take a statement from me four years ago.','withdraw your statement (= say that a statement you gave is not true ) She later withdrew her statement.','a short/brief statement Police last night issued a brief statement about the incident.','a clear statement (= giving an opinion clearly ) The article was a clear statement of his beliefs.','a sweeping statement (= one that is too general ) Researchers do not want to make any sweeping statements at this stage.','a false/misleading statement (= one that is not true ) She is accused of making false statements to obtain a passport.','an official statement The company is expected to make an official statement tomorrow.','a formal statement (= one you must sign to show that it is true ) You will be asked to make a formal statement.','a public statement (= one made in public ) We will be making no public statements about the matter.','a written statement One neighbour said in a written statement that she often heard a baby ‘crying for help’.','a prepared statement (= one that is prepared and then read out ) His solicitor read a prepared statement on his behalf.','a sworn statement (= one that you officially promise is true ) The reports were based on sworn statements of graduates of the terrorist training camp.','a policy statement (= one that explains a government policy ) In his first major policy statement to Parliament he promised to end corruption in public life.','a mission statement (= one in which an organization states its aims ) The role of a mission statement is to focus on the purpose of the organization.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The type of car you drive makes a statement about you.","translation":"نوع ماشینی که می‌رانید بیانگر شماست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001652181.mp3"},{"sentence":"a fashion statement","translation":"یک بیانیه مد","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001782263.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('8c9bd6f4-9d2e-51cd-b3c4-9693b5329e2c','bb2f5b36-2f63-555f-bc9c-c60ae5c6bf9e',4,null,null,'formal','the act of expressing something in words','[ uncountable ]',null,'عمل بیان چیزی در کلمات','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make a statement (= say something, especially in public ) The minister will make a statement on the matter tomorrow.','give a statement (= make a statement, especially to the police ) He gave a statement to the police.','issue/release/put out a statement (= give a written statement to newspapers, TV etc ) The Russian Foreign Ministry issued a short statement saying the meeting was ‘useful’.','take/get a statement from somebody I asked the police why they didn’t take a statement from me four years ago.','withdraw your statement (= say that a statement you gave is not true ) She later withdrew her statement.','a short/brief statement Police last night issued a brief statement about the incident.','a clear statement (= giving an opinion clearly ) The article was a clear statement of his beliefs.','a sweeping statement (= one that is too general ) Researchers do not want to make any sweeping statements at this stage.','a false/misleading statement (= one that is not true ) She is accused of making false statements to obtain a passport.','an official statement The company is expected to make an official statement tomorrow.','a formal statement (= one you must sign to show that it is true ) You will be asked to make a formal statement.','a public statement (= one made in public ) We will be making no public statements about the matter.','a written statement One neighbour said in a written statement that she often heard a baby ‘crying for help’.','a prepared statement (= one that is prepared and then read out ) His solicitor read a prepared statement on his behalf.','a sworn statement (= one that you officially promise is true ) The reports were based on sworn statements of graduates of the terrorist training camp.','a policy statement (= one that explains a government policy ) In his first major policy statement to Parliament he promised to end corruption in public life.','a mission statement (= one in which an organization states its aims ) The role of a mission statement is to focus on the purpose of the organization.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"presentation and clarity of statement","translation":"ارائه و وضوح بیانیه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001652186.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
