('2455030a-77e7-592e-99a2-85f859f6b6b1','883f303c-657a-55f2-aadc-06ac2bbee15b',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to accept that you are responsible for a piece of work, and start to do it',null,null,'پذیرفتن (مسئولیت)؛ متقبل شدن (کار)؛ عهده‌دار شدن (کار)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['undertake a task/project Every task he undertook was tackled with great determination.','undertake work The work is being undertaken by team of experts.','undertake research/a study Students may undertake full-time supervised research leading to the award of a Ph.D.','undertake a review/analysis The Court of Appeal decided to undertake a review of the Law.','undertake a journey/voyage You should not undertake a long journey if you are unwell.','undertake duties (= do things as part of your job ) I’m rarely asked to undertake teaching duties these days.','something is not to be undertaken lightly (= not to be started without serious thought, for example because it is difficult ) It was not a voyage to be undertaken lightly.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Dr Johnson undertook the task of writing a comprehensive English dictionary.","translation":"دکتر جانسون وظیفه نوشتن یک فرهنگ لغت انگلیسی جامع را بر عهده گرفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001587884.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
