('0c7693bb-0654-544a-bf30-7696c765fde1','38e73de3-906b-5daa-9d4d-98fa642b3f0e',4,null,null,'spoken & written','the final arrangement of an agreement , a business deal etc','[ uncountable ]',null,'ترتیب نهایی یک توافق، یک معامله تجاری و غیره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['come to/arrive at/reach a conclusion (= decide something ) I eventually came to the conclusion that I wanted to study law.','draw a conclusion (= decide something from what you learn or see ) We tried not to draw any conclusions too early in the investigation.','jump to/leap to conclusions (= decide something is true without knowing all the facts, especially when you are wrong ) Everyone jumped to the conclusion that we would get married.','lead to/point to a conclusion (= make you decide that something is true ) All the data led to only one conclusion.','support a conclusion (= suggest that something is true ) The evidence supports the conclusion that his death was an accident.','an obvious conclusion All her symptoms led to the obvious conclusion – she was pregnant.','the wrong conclusion Reporters saw the couple together and leapt to the wrong conclusion.','the right/correct conclusion I am sure that you came to the right conclusion.','the opposite conclusion A lot of scientific evidence supports the opposite conclusion.','the inescapable/inevitable conclusion (= one that is very obvious, although you may not like it ) The inescapable conclusion was that the country needed a change of leadership.','the logical conclusion (= one that makes sense when you think about it carefully ) The logical conclusion is that short commercials are just as effective as longer ones.','a firm conclusion (= definite decision ) At the end of the day, no firm conclusion had been reached.','a surprising/startling conclusion After years of research, he reached a startling conclusion.','a hasty conclusion (= one that you reach too quickly, so that you are probably wrong ) Researchers must beware of drawing hasty conclusions.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the conclusion of a peace treaty","translation":"انعقاد پیمان صلح","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000852333.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('835d04c5-064b-5e86-8cbd-dc496009c916','38e73de3-906b-5daa-9d4d-98fa642b3f0e',5,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'be a foregone conclusion','نتیجه‌گیری؛ پایان (نوشته)؛ عقد قرارداد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['come to/arrive at/reach a conclusion (= decide something ) I eventually came to the conclusion that I wanted to study law.','draw a conclusion (= decide something from what you learn or see ) We tried not to draw any conclusions too early in the investigation.','jump to/leap to conclusions (= decide something is true without knowing all the facts, especially when you are wrong ) Everyone jumped to the conclusion that we would get married.','lead to/point to a conclusion (= make you decide that something is true ) All the data led to only one conclusion.','support a conclusion (= suggest that something is true ) The evidence supports the conclusion that his death was an accident.','an obvious conclusion All her symptoms led to the obvious conclusion – she was pregnant.','the wrong conclusion Reporters saw the couple together and leapt to the wrong conclusion.','the right/correct conclusion I am sure that you came to the right conclusion.','the opposite conclusion A lot of scientific evidence supports the opposite conclusion.','the inescapable/inevitable conclusion (= one that is very obvious, although you may not like it ) The inescapable conclusion was that the country needed a change of leadership.','the logical conclusion (= one that makes sense when you think about it carefully ) The logical conclusion is that short commercials are just as effective as longer ones.','a firm conclusion (= definite decision ) At the end of the day, no firm conclusion had been reached.','a surprising/startling conclusion After years of research, he reached a startling conclusion.','a hasty conclusion (= one that you reach too quickly, so that you are probably wrong ) Researchers must beware of drawing hasty conclusions.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('b4d54844-3a56-58c4-ace6-652940f5fe86','ffb94dca-2640-5041-99c2-c3153798b7bb',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a large formal meeting where a lot of people discuss important matters such as business, politics , or science , especially for several days',null,'press conference','کنفرانس، همایش؛ نشست رسمی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['go to a conference ( also attend a conference formal ) Hundreds of delegates are attending the conference.','hold a conference (= have one ) Their annual conference was held in Chicago.','host a conference (= have it in your country ) In June, Japan hosted a peace conference.','organize a conference The administration organized a conference on Africa.','convene a conference formal (= arrange one ) a national conference on school violence convened by the U. S. Department of Education','address a conference (= give a speech at one ) He received a warm welcome when he addressed the conference.','a peace/climate/sales etc conference an international climate conference in Sweden','a world/international conference the world conference on human rights','a national conference Brazil’s national conference on health','a regional conference In Northern Africa, there have been important regional conferences on education.','an annual conference the biggest annual conference for teachers of English','a party conference (= for a particular political party ) the Labour party conference','a summit conference (= for the leaders of governments ) The heads of most Arab states met in Amman for a summit conference.','conference facilities The hotel has conference facilities for 100 people.','a conference centre (= a building or group of buildings used for conferences )','a conference hall Thousands of people demonstrated outside the conference hall, demanding government action.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Representatives from over 100 countries attended the International Peace Conference in Geneva.","translation":"نمایندگان بیش از 100 کشور در کنفرانس بین المللی صلح در ژنو شرکت کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001101791.mp3"},{"sentence":"a UN conference on the environment","translation":"کنفرانس سازمان ملل در مورد محیط زیست","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001101784.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('e36f2ca7-49c6-5e4d-86c5-7a6d42fa70fe','ffb94dca-2640-5041-99c2-c3153798b7bb',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a private meeting for a few people to have formal discussions',null,null,'یک جلسه خصوصی برای چند نفر برای گفتگوهای رسمی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['go to a conference ( also attend a conference formal ) Hundreds of delegates are attending the conference.','hold a conference (= have one ) Their annual conference was held in Chicago.','host a conference (= have it in your country ) In June, Japan hosted a peace conference.','organize a conference The administration organized a conference on Africa.','convene a conference formal (= arrange one ) a national conference on school violence convened by the U. S. Department of Education','address a conference (= give a speech at one ) He received a warm welcome when he addressed the conference.','a peace/climate/sales etc conference an international climate conference in Sweden','a world/international conference the world conference on human rights','a national conference Brazil’s national conference on health','a regional conference In Northern Africa, there have been important regional conferences on education.','an annual conference the biggest annual conference for teachers of English','a party conference (= for a particular political party ) the Labour party conference','a summit conference (= for the leaders of governments ) The heads of most Arab states met in Amman for a summit conference.','conference facilities The hotel has conference facilities for 100 people.','a conference centre (= a building or group of buildings used for conferences )','a conference hall Thousands of people demonstrated outside the conference hall, demanding government action.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"After a brief conference with his aides, he left for the airport.","translation":"او پس از یک کنفرانس کوتاه با دستیارانش راهی فرودگاه شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001101805.mp3"},{"sentence":"The meeting will be held in the conference room at 10 am.","translation":"این جلسه ساعت 10 صبح در سالن کنفرانس برگزار می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717227.mp3"},{"sentence":"Mr Dickson is in conference.","translation":"آقای دیکسون در کنفرانس است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717230.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('ebb11135-04d6-5693-b8b6-53076f690137','ffb94dca-2640-5041-99c2-c3153798b7bb',3,null,null,'spoken & written','a group of teams that play against each other to see who is the best',null,null,'گروهی از تیم ها که با یکدیگر بازی می کنند تا ببینند چه کسی بهترین است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['go to a conference ( also attend a conference formal ) Hundreds of delegates are attending the conference.','hold a conference (= have one ) Their annual conference was held in Chicago.','host a conference (= have it in your country ) In June, Japan hosted a peace conference.','organize a conference The administration organized a conference on Africa.','convene a conference formal (= arrange one ) a national conference on school violence convened by the U. S. Department of Education','address a conference (= give a speech at one ) He received a warm welcome when he addressed the conference.','a peace/climate/sales etc conference an international climate conference in Sweden','a world/international conference the world conference on human rights','a national conference Brazil’s national conference on health','a regional conference In Northern Africa, there have been important regional conferences on education.','an annual conference the biggest annual conference for teachers of English','a party conference (= for a particular political party ) the Labour party conference','a summit conference (= for the leaders of governments ) The heads of most Arab states met in Amman for a summit conference.','conference facilities The hotel has conference facilities for 100 people.','a conference centre (= a building or group of buildings used for conferences )','a conference hall Thousands of people demonstrated outside the conference hall, demanding government action.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the Western Conference finals","translation":"فینال کنفرانس غرب","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001101822.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('1df9b0bc-0008-5e53-a429-157fb3f6c4ff','db067593-d407-58e5-8353-68674a362526',1,'feeling somebody/something is good','احساس کسی / چیزی خوب است','spoken & written','the feeling that you can trust someone or something to be good, work well, or produce good results','[ uncountable ]',null,'اطمینان، اعتماد؛ اطمینان نفس (خودباوری)؛ راز','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have confidence in somebody/something The people no longer have any confidence in their government.','lose confidence in somebody/something Employees are losing confidence in the company.','gain/win somebody’s confidence As team captain, he soon won the confidence of the players.','inspire confidence (= make people have confidence ) Our education system should inspire public confidence.','restore confidence (= make people have confidence again ) Interest rate reductions would restore business confidence.','boost confidence (= make people have more confidence ) The government is keen to boost consumer confidence and spending.','shake somebody’s confidence (= make them have less confidence ) The stock market fall has shaken the confidence of investors.','undermine/damage/weaken somebody’s confidence (= make someone have less confidence ) The situation in the US was undermining foreign confidence in the dollar.','destroy/shatter confidence in somebody/something A further crisis has destroyed public confidence in the bank.','have every/complete/absolute confidence in somebody/something A manager must be able to have complete confidence in his staff.','a lack of confidence the public’s lack of confidence in the National Health Service','a crisis of confidence (= a situation in which people no longer trust a government, system etc ) the crisis of confidence over food safety','public confidence The changes should improve public confidence in the system.','consumer confidence (= that ordinary people have when the economic situation is good ) Consumer confidence has fallen to its lowest for two years.','business confidence (= that businesses have when the economic situation is good ) The region has gained 46,000 jobs and business confidence is high.','investor confidence (= that investors have when the economic situation is good ) A fall in the value of shares damages investor confidence.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Public confidence in the government is at an all-time low.","translation":"اعتماد عمومی به دولت به پایین ترین حد خود رسیده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717274.mp3"},{"sentence":"She had complete confidence in the doctors.","translation":"او به پزشکان اطمینان کامل داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001939825.mp3"},{"sentence":"Opinion polls show that voters have lost confidence in the administration.","translation":"نظرسنجی ها نشان می دهد که رای دهندگان اعتماد خود را به دولت از دست داده اند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001101907.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('69e5319d-852f-52c5-889b-3b0ad57d4797','db067593-d407-58e5-8353-68674a362526',2,'belief in yourself','باور به خود','spoken & written','the belief that you have the ability to do things well or deal with situations successfully','[ uncountable ]',null,'این باور که شما توانایی انجام کارها را به خوبی یا کنار آمدن با موقعیت ها با موفقیت دارید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I didn’t have any confidence in myself.","translation":"هیچ اعتمادی به خودم نداشتم","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717295.mp3"},{"sentence":"Good training will give a beginner the confidence to enjoy skiing.","translation":"تمرین خوب به یک مبتدی اعتماد به نفس برای لذت بردن از اسکی می دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717308.mp3"},{"sentence":"I felt I was doing well and my confidence began to grow.","translation":"احساس کردم که خوب کار می کنم و اعتماد به نفسم شروع به رشد کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717312.mp3"},{"sentence":"Our goal is to prepare students to go into the business world with confidence.","translation":"هدف ما این است که دانشجویان را آماده کنیم تا با اعتماد به نفس وارد دنیای تجارت شوند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717315.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('a3a761a2-0d78-5e59-a7d7-72fe732a3d54','db067593-d407-58e5-8353-68674a362526',3,'feeling something is true','احساس چیزی درست است','spoken & written','the feeling that something is definite or true','[ uncountable ]',null,'احساس اینکه چیزی قطعی یا واقعی است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"How can anyone say with confidence that the recession is over?","translation":"چگونه کسی می تواند با اطمینان بگوید که رکود به پایان رسیده است؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001101947.mp3"},{"sentence":"I have complete confidence in Mr Wright’s analysis of the situation.","translation":"من به تحلیل آقای رایت از وضعیت اطمینان کامل دارم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717321.mp3"},{"sentence":"I have every confidence that the job will be completed satisfactorily on time.","translation":"من کاملاً اطمینان دارم که کار در زمان مقرر به طور رضایت بخشی انجام می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001101950.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('4a1cd35e-96c2-5361-a702-8d200c2f908d','db067593-d407-58e5-8353-68674a362526',4,'keep information secret','اطلاعات را مخفی نگه دارید','spoken & written','if you tell someone something in confidence, you tell them something on the understanding that they will not tell anyone else','[ uncountable ]',null,'اگر محرمانه به کسی چیزی بگویید، با درک و فهم به او چیزی می گویید که به دیگران نگویند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I’ll tell you about Moira – in confidence, of course.","translation":"من در مورد مویرا به شما خواهم گفت - البته با اطمینان.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717335.mp3"},{"sentence":"Any information given during the interview will be treated in the strictest confidence .","translation":"هر گونه اطلاعاتی که در طول مصاحبه داده می شود، در نهایت محرمانه بودن رفتار خواهد شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717341.mp3"},{"sentence":"Lawyers are satisfied that no breach of confidence took place.","translation":"وکلا راضی هستند که هیچ نقض اعتماد صورت نگرفته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717349.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('4ab0b6da-95ff-5da1-9c6d-845b5eb1bd8e','db067593-d407-58e5-8353-68674a362526',5,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'take somebody into your confidence','اطمینان، اعتماد؛ اطمینان نفس (خودباوری)؛ راز','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('c1815a40-a1d2-5145-8771-d962873a62ae','db067593-d407-58e5-8353-68674a362526',6,'a secret','یک راز','spoken & written','a secret or a piece of information that is private or personal','[ countable ]',null,'راز یا بخشی از اطلاعات که خصوصی یا شخصی است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"They spent their evenings drinking wine and sharing confidences.","translation":"آنها شب های خود را با نوشیدن شراب و به اشتراک گذاشتن اعتماد به نفس می گذراندند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001101975.mp3"},{"sentence":"I have never betrayed a confidence .","translation":"من هرگز به یک اعتماد به نفس خیانت نکرده ام.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001717360.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('53e84872-527e-5612-b9f2-877d8ae07714','98aa3d5e-e03b-541c-b708-e0848952663f',1,'relationship','رابطه','spoken & written','the way in which two facts , ideas, events etc are related to each other, and one is affected or caused by the other','[ countable ]',null,'ارتباط، پیوند؛ وسایل ارتباطی؛ آشنایان',array['link']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a connection (with/to something) A lot of social problems have a direct connection to alcohol or drug use.','see a connection It''s easy to see a connection between stress and illness.','make a connection In learning to read, children make a connection between a written sign and a known sound or word.','establish a connection (= show that there is one ) Scientists have attempted to establish a connection between these two theories.','discover/find a connection This is the first official investigation to find a connection.','something suggests a connection There is nothing to suggest a connection between the hospital food and the illness.','break a connection (= stop it existing ) We must break the connection between money and politics.','sever a connection (= break it ) We cannot sever our connection with the past.','a direct connection Many people see a direct connection between these events.','a close/strong connection the close connection between maths and physics','an intimate connection (= a very close connection ) There is an intimate connection between political liberty and economic freedom.','a causal connection (= that causes or is caused by something else ) Psychologists have established a causal connection between behaviour and rewards.','a clear/obvious connection There is an obvious connection between this painting and his earlier works.','a loose connection ( also a tenuous connection formal ) (= one that is not strong, close, or obvious ) There seemed to be only a loose connection between the questions and the answers.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the causal connection between smoking and cancer","translation":"ارتباط علی بین سیگار کشیدن و سرطان","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001103643.mp3"},{"sentence":"There is a connection between pollution and the death of trees.","translation":"بین آلودگی و مرگ درختان ارتباط وجود دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001845311.mp3"},{"sentence":"Mr O''Hara had no known connection with terrorist activity.","translation":"آقای اوهارا هیچ ارتباطی با فعالیت های تروریستی نداشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001103646.mp3"},{"sentence":"Williams apparently has no connection to the case.","translation":"ظاهرا ویلیامز هیچ ارتباطی با این پرونده ندارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001845316.mp3"},{"sentence":"Police have so far failed to establish a connection between the two murders.","translation":"پلیس تاکنون نتوانسته ارتباطی بین این دو قتل ایجاد کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001103650.mp3"},{"sentence":"The evidence was there in the file but no one made the connection .","translation":"شواهد در پرونده وجود داشت اما هیچ کس ارتباط را برقرار نکرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001103654.mp3"},{"sentence":"Students often see little connection between school and the rest of their lives.","translation":"دانش آموزان اغلب ارتباط کمی بین مدرسه و بقیه زندگی خود می بینند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001845318.mp3"},{"sentence":"He demonstrated the close connection between social conditions and health.","translation":"او ارتباط نزدیک بین شرایط اجتماعی و سلامت را نشان داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001939846.mp3"}]'::jsonb,8),
('ec926d73-b0dc-5fe9-99a0-ade1724727eb','98aa3d5e-e03b-541c-b708-e0848952663f',2,'joining','پیوستن','spoken & written','when two or more things are joined together or when something is joined to a larger system or network','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'هنگامی که دو یا چند چیز به یکدیگر متصل می شوند یا زمانی که چیزی به یک سیستم یا شبکه بزرگتر متصل می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a connection (with/to something) A lot of social problems have a direct connection to alcohol or drug use.','see a connection It''s easy to see a connection between stress and illness.','make a connection In learning to read, children make a connection between a written sign and a known sound or word.','establish a connection (= show that there is one ) Scientists have attempted to establish a connection between these two theories.','discover/find a connection This is the first official investigation to find a connection.','something suggests a connection There is nothing to suggest a connection between the hospital food and the illness.','break a connection (= stop it existing ) We must break the connection between money and politics.','sever a connection (= break it ) We cannot sever our connection with the past.','a direct connection Many people see a direct connection between these events.','a close/strong connection the close connection between maths and physics','an intimate connection (= a very close connection ) There is an intimate connection between political liberty and economic freedom.','a causal connection (= that causes or is caused by something else ) Psychologists have established a causal connection between behaviour and rewards.','a clear/obvious connection There is an obvious connection between this painting and his earlier works.','a loose connection ( also a tenuous connection formal ) (= one that is not strong, close, or obvious ) There seemed to be only a loose connection between the questions and the answers.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a digital telephone connection via satellite","translation":"اتصال تلفن دیجیتال از طریق ماهواره","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001675354.mp3"},{"sentence":"They’re offering free Internet connection.","translation":"آنها اتصال اینترنت رایگان را ارائه می دهند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001675355.mp3"},{"sentence":"The socket allows connection to a PC.","translation":"سوکت امکان اتصال به کامپیوتر را فراهم می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001675361.mp3"},{"sentence":"There’s a £25 connection charge (= money you pay to be connected to a service such as telephones, electricity etc ) .","translation":"هزینه اتصال 25 پوند (= پولی که برای اتصال به خدماتی مانند تلفن، برق و غیره می پردازید) وجود دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001675362.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
